    "fullDescription": "The Integral Coach Factory (ICF), Chennai, a premier manufacturing unit under the Ministry of Railways, has published an official notification for the engagement of Trade Apprentices under the Apprentices Act 1961 for 1,010 vacancies across various trades including Fitter, Machinist, Electrician, Welder, Painter, and Carpenter. Applicants must have passed their 10th standard examination with a minimum of 50% marks and hold a National Trade Certificate (ITI) issued by NCVT/SCVT in the relevant trade. Selection for these apprenticeship positions is conducted entirely on the basis of a merit list formed by taking the average of marks obtained in both the Matriculation and ITI examinations. Selected apprentices undergo rigorous hands-on technical training at the ICF manufacturing facility, receiving a monthly stipend as prescribed by the Railway Board. This apprenticeship serves as a valuable stepping stone for candidates seeking future employment opportunities within the Indian Railways sector. Interested candidates should review the trade-wise vacancy breakdown and submit their applications before the stipulated deadline.",
