    "fullContent": "### Portal Launch Overview On September 4, 2026, the Union Minister for Environment, Forest and Climate Change inaugurated **PRANA 2.0** (Portal for Regulation of Air-pollution in Non-Attainment cities). The upgraded platform modernizes air quality governance across **131 non-attainment cities** identified under the **National Clean Air Programme (NCAP)**. ### Enhanced Features of PRANA 2.0 * **AI Predictive Analytics:** Utilizes machine learning to forecast hyper-local Particulate Matter (PM2.5 and PM10) spikes up to 72 hours in advance, allowing local authorities to trigger emergency measures. * **Satellite Data Integration:** Seamlessly syncs with ISRO Earth Observation satellites and ground-based Continuous Ambient Air Quality Monitoring Stations (CAAQMS). * **Grant Tracking Module:** Tracks transparent utilization of the 15th Finance Commission performance-based grants allocated for urban clean air initiatives. ### Targets under NCAP NCAP initially aimed for a 20-30% reduction in PM levels by 2024, which was extended to a target of **up to 40% reduction by 2026** (compared to 2017 base levels). PRANA 2.0 will evaluate final achievement compliance for all targeted cities. ### Exam Relevance * **Environment & Ecology:** National Clean Air Programme (NCAP) parameters, CAAQMS, Non-attainment cities definition. * **E-Governance:** PRANA portal functionality and inter-departmental climate actions.",
