    "fullContent": "### Missile Test Overview On September 4, 2026, the **Defence Research and Development Organisation (DRDO)**, alongside the Indian Army, conducted consecutive flight tests of the 4th-generation **Very Short Range Air Defence System (VSHORADS)** missile off the coast of Odisha at Integrated Test Range (ITR), Chandipur. The test targets—high-speed unmanned aerial vehicles mimicking low-altitude threats—were successfully intercepted and neutralized. ### Technical & Operational Features * **System Type:** Man-Portable Air Defence System (MANPADS), optimized for neutralising low-altitude aerial threats such as drones, helicopters, and low-flying jets. * **Guidance System:** Incorporates an advanced **uncooled Imaging Infrared (IIR) seeker**, eliminating the need for bulky coolant systems and enabling rapid deployment in field conditions. * **Propulsion:** Powered by a dual-thrust solid reaction motor, offering swift acceleration and terminal maneuverability. * **Development:** Lead laboratory **Research Centre Imarat (RCI), Hyderabad**, in collaboration with other DRDO facilities and Indian industry partners. ### Operational Significance The induction of VSHORADS will bolster the Indian Armed Forces' air defense capabilities along rugged high-altitude borders (such as LAC and LOC), providing immediate field defense for ground infantry formations. ### Exam Relevance * **Defense Tech for Exams:** Classifications of missile defense (VSHORADS, QRSAM, MRSAM, LRSAM). * **Developer Knowledge:** DRDO’s RCI Hyderabad role in missile guidance systems.",
