    "fullContent": "### Institutional Update The **Reserve Bank of India (RBI)** has launched nationwide offline capabilities for both retail (e₹-R) and wholesale (e₹-W) Central Bank Digital Currency (CBDC). Announced by the RBI Governor during the Monetary Policy Committee briefing backdrop, this update enables seamless peer-to-peer (P2P) and peer-to-merchant (P2M) transactions without an internet connection. ### Technological Architecture * **NFC Proximity Payments:** Smart devices equipped with Near Field Communication chips can execute instant token transfers directly between secure hardware elements. * **USSD for Feature Phones:** Non-smartphone users can initiate e₹ payments using standard `*99#` USSD protocols, ensuring equity in digital financial access. * **Offline Capping:** To manage operational risk and security, the single offline transaction limit is fixed at **₹2,000**, with an overall wallet offline ceiling of **₹5,000** before online re-verification is required. ### Impact on Financial Inclusion This development addresses transaction drop-offs in rural and hilly terrains with weak telecommunication networks. By removing dependency on telecom coverage, the e-Rupee moves closer to replicating the physical characteristics of cash while retaining digital traceability. ### Exam Relevance * **Banking & Financial Awareness:** Difference between UPI (account-to-account transfer) and CBDC (legal tender digital token directly backed by RBI liability). * **Tech Terminology:** Near Field Communication (NFC), Programmable CBDC, USSD.",
